  },
  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Your phone can recognize your face, and AI can write a poem. But how does a computer actually learn anything?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "brain",
          "label": "LEARN?"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "robot",
          "label": "COMPUTER"
        },
        "subtitle": "How AI learns",
        "mid": "?"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Great question! Nobody types in all the rules. Instead, the AI learns from lots of examples, a bit like we do.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "book",
        "text": "Learns from examples",
        "cue": "examples"
      },
      "punch": "examples"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So what are we going to find out today?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Four things. What a neural network is, how its layers work, how it learns from mistakes, and why training data matters so much.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "TODAY",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Neural networks",
            "icon": "brain",
            "cue": "neural"
          },
          {
            "label": "Layers",
            "icon": "target",
            "cue": "layers"
          },
          {
            "label": "Learning from mistakes",
            "icon": "check",
            "cue": "mistakes"
          },
          {
            "label": "Training data",
            "icon": "book",
            "cue": "data"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Okay, start with the name. Neural network. Is there a real brain inside the computer?",
      "chapter": "What is a neural network?",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🧠",
        "text": "A real brain?",
        "cue": "brain"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "No. It's inspired by brain cells called neurons, but it's really just math running on a computer.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "BRAIN",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Real neurons",
              "icon": "brain",
              "cue": "neurons"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "NEURAL NETWORK",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Math on a computer",
              "icon": "robot",
              "cue": "math",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Math? What kind of math?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Simple math, but lots of it. Each tiny unit takes in numbers, mixes them using weights, and passes a new number along.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "ONE TINY UNIT",
        "traveler": "🔢",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "📥",
            "label": "Numbers in",
            "cue": "takes"
          },
          {
            "icon": "⚖️",
            "label": "Mix with weights",
            "cue": "weights"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📤",
            "label": "Pass it on",
            "cue": "passes"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Weights? Like at the gym?",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🏋️",
        "text": "Weights?",
        "cue": "weights"
      },
      "punch": "gym"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Ha, no. Think of a weight as a dial. Turn it up, and that input matters more. Turn it down, and it matters less.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "DIAL UP",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Matters more",
              "icon": "check",
              "cue": "more",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "DIAL DOWN",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Matters less",
              "icon": "x",
              "cue": "less"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And how many dials are there?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "In big modern AI, there can be billions. Nobody sets them by hand. The network finds good settings by itself, during training.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎛️",
        "text": "Billions of dials",
        "cue": "billions",
        "sub": "Set by training",
        "sub_cue": "training"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "You keep saying layers. Why does it need layers?",
      "chapter": "Layers",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🥞",
        "text": "Why layers?",
        "cue": "layers"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Because the units are stacked. Each layer passes its results to the next, so the network builds up from simple to complex.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "STACKED LAYERS",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Input layer",
            "icon": "doc",
            "cue": "stacked"
          },
          {
            "label": "Middle layers",
            "icon": "brain",
            "cue": "passes"
          },
          {
            "label": "Output",
            "icon": "target",
            "cue": "complex"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Show me with an example. Say, a photo of a cat.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐱",
        "text": "Example: a cat photo",
        "cue": "cat"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Early layers spot simple things, like edges and colors. Middle layers combine those into shapes, like ears and eyes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "LAYER BY LAYER",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Edges & colors",
            "icon": "eye",
            "cue": "edges"
          },
          {
            "label": "Shapes: ears, eyes",
            "icon": "target",
            "cue": "shapes"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Then the last layers put it all together and say: this is probably a cat.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "check",
        "text": "Probably a cat!",
        "cue": "probably"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Probably? It isn't sure?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Right. It gives a best guess with a confidence score. Like, mostly cat, a little bit dog.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "CAT",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Most likely",
              "icon": "check",
              "cue": "mostly",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "DOG",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A little",
              "icon": "x",
              "cue": "little"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So it can be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes, especially with unusual pictures, like a cat in a costume. That's why we still double-check what AI tells us.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Unusual = tricky",
        "cue": "unusual",
        "sub": "Double-check AI",
        "sub_cue": "double-check"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Okay, here's the big one. How does it learn in the first place?",
      "chapter": "Learning from mistakes",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "x",
          "label": "WRONG"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "check",
          "label": "RIGHT"
        },
        "subtitle": "Learning from mistakes",
        "mid": "→"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "At the start, all the dials are set randomly. So its first guesses are basically nonsense.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎲",
        "text": "Random dials at first",
        "cue": "randomly"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Then what?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "It looks at an example, like a photo labeled cat, and makes a guess. Then it checks the guess against the right answer.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "ONE EXAMPLE",
        "traveler": "🖼️",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🏷️",
            "label": "Labeled photo",
            "cue": "labeled"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🤔",
            "label": "Make a guess",
            "cue": "guess"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Check the answer",
            "cue": "checks"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And if it's wrong?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "It measures how wrong it was, then nudges every dial a tiny bit in the direction that makes the answer less wrong.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎛️",
        "text": "Nudge the dials",
        "cue": "nudges",
        "sub": "A tiny bit",
        "sub_cue": "tiny"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Just a tiny bit? Why not fix it all at once?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Big jumps would mess up what it learned before. Small steps, over and over, slowly add up to something smart.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "BIG JUMPS",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Mess up old lessons",
              "icon": "x",
              "cue": "mess"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "SMALL STEPS",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Slowly get smart",
              "icon": "check",
              "cue": "slowly",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So it's a loop."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Exactly. Guess, check, adjust, repeat. Millions of times, with lots of examples. That loop is what we call training.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "TRAINING LOOP",
        "center": "🧠",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🤔",
            "label": "Guess",
            "cue": "guess"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Check",
            "cue": "check"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🎛️",
            "label": "Adjust",
            "cue": "adjust"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔁",
            "label": "Repeat",
            "cue": "repeat"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      },
      "punch": "training"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "That's a bit like me learning to throw darts.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎯",
        "text": "Like learning darts",
        "cue": "darts"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Totally! You throw, see where it lands, adjust your aim, and throw again. The AI just does it with math instead of muscles.",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "DARTS LOOP",
        "center": "🎯",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "✋",
            "label": "Throw",
            "cue": "throw"
          },
          {
            "icon": "👀",
            "label": "See where it lands",
            "cue": "see"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💪",
            "label": "Adjust your aim",
            "cue": "adjust"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Where do all those examples come from?",
      "chapter": "Why data matters",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "book",
        "text": "Examples from where?",
        "cue": "examples"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "People collect them. Photos with labels, text from books and websites, recordings of speech. That's called training data.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "TRAINING DATA",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Labeled photos",
            "icon": "eye",
            "cue": "photos"
          },
          {
            "label": "Text",
            "icon": "book",
            "cue": "text"
          },
          {
            "label": "Speech recordings",
            "icon": "phone",
            "cue": "recordings"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#8E44AD"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Does it matter what's in there?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Hugely. An AI can only learn from what it sees. If the examples are wrong or one-sided, it learns those mistakes too.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Bad data, bad AI",
        "cue": "wrong"
      },
      "punch": "hugely"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Give me an example."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Say you only show it photos of orange cats. Later, it might not recognize a black cat as a cat at all.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "TRAINED ON",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Only orange cats",
              "icon": "🟠",
              "cue": "orange"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "MIGHT MISS",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "A black cat",
              "icon": "⚫",
              "cue": "black"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So that's where unfair AI can come from?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Often, yes. That's why builders try to use varied, fair data, and why people keep testing AI after it's built.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Better AI needs",
        "icon": "shield",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Varied data",
            "cue": "varied",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Fair data",
            "cue": "fair",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Ongoing testing",
            "cue": "testing",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Once it's trained, does it keep learning from me while I use it?",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "phone",
        "text": "Learning from me?",
        "cue": "learning"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Usually not on the spot. Training happens first, on powerful computers. When you use the app, the dials are mostly fixed.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "TRAINING",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Slow, huge computers",
              "icon": "warn",
              "cue": "training"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "USING IT",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Quick, dials fixed",
              "icon": "check",
              "cue": "fixed",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "But some companies may use chats to train future versions. So check the settings, and keep private info out.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Your chats",
        "icon": "lock",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Check the settings",
            "cue": "settings",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Keep private info out",
            "cue": "private",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Quiz time, Dad! Question one. At the very start of training, how are the dials set? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Quiz time!",
        "cue": "quiz",
        "sub": "Dials at the start?",
        "sub_cue": "dials"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Randomly! So the first guesses are nonsense.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎲",
        "text": "Randomly!",
        "cue": "randomly"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Correct! Question two. What are the four steps of the training loop? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔁",
        "text": "The training loop?",
        "cue": "training"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Guess, check, adjust, and repeat!",
      "board": {
        "type": "cycle",
        "title": "TRAINING LOOP",
        "center": "🧠",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🤔",
            "label": "Guess",
            "cue": "guess"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Check",
            "cue": "check"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🎛️",
            "label": "Adjust",
            "cue": "adjust"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔁",
            "label": "Repeat",
            "cue": "repeat"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes! Last one. If an AI only ever sees orange cats, what might go wrong? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🐈",
        "text": "Only orange cats?",
        "cue": "orange"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "It might not recognize other cats. Bad data, bad results.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "check",
        "text": "Bad data, bad results",
        "cue": "bad"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So: layers of dials, a guess-and-check loop, and good data.",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "text": "LAYERS OF DIALS",
            "icon": "brain",
            "cue": "layers",
            "color": "#0A84FF"
          },
          {
            "text": "GUESS, CHECK, ADJUST",
            "icon": "🔁",
            "cue": "guess",
            "color": "#E91E63"
          },
          {
            "text": "GOOD DATA MATTERS",
            "icon": "book",
            "cue": "data",
            "color": "#2ECC71"
          }
        ]
      },
      "punch": "loop"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Perfect score! And remember, it's math, not magic. It learns patterns, and it can still make mistakes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "bulb",
        "text": "Math, not magic",
        "cue": "math"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "You got it! Subscribe to AI Nation Studio, and share this with a friend! And next time your phone recognizes a face... can you explain how it learned?"
    }
  ]
}